1. Land and building values. Does the extract show land assessed value and =
building (improvement) assessed value as separate fields, or only a total? =
This is the field I most need. Separate and Total

2. Tax years. Does it contain the reassessed values for tax year 2026? Can =
it also include the tax year 2025 values (1968 base year), in the same file=
 or as a second file? 2 files needed for multiple tax years. 2026 file show=
s value on day of file run. 2025 file would be the final value at EOY. This=
 would be the last value prior to the new reassessed values

3. Certified versus current values. Are the 2026 values as certified in Nov=
ember 2025 for billing, or as they stand today after appeals? If only curre=
nt values are available, is there a field showing which parcels were change=
d on appeal? Current Value only

4. Other fields. Does the extract include:
- parcel ID
- municipality and school district
- property class or land-use code
- exemption status or code, and taxable value
- homestead/farmstead exclusion status
- property address
- owner name and mailing address
- lot size or acreage
Yes. Land SqFt and Acreage if available

5. Code tables. Does it come with a data dictionary or code tables for the =
class and exemption codes? Yes

6. Format and scope. Is the file CSV or Excel? Is it countywide, or can it =
be limited to the City of Scranton? Either one works for me. A list of the =
column names, or a few sample rows, would answer most of these questions at=
 once. County Wide

7. Cost and timing. With email delivery, is $600 the total cost? About how =
long after the check arrives does the file go out? $600 per tax year. Withi=
n a few days.



