<p class=3D"MsoNormal">Dear Ms. Harte,<br>
<br>
Thank you for the response and the IT request form. Before I submit the for=
m and payment, I have a few questions about what the one-time extract conta=
ins. Could you forward this to Ryan or Leeann in the IT Department, or send=
 me their email address so I can
 ask them directly?<br>
<br>
1. Land and building values. Does the extract show land assessed value and =
building (improvement) assessed value as separate fields, or only a total? =
This is the field I most need.
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">Separate and Total</span></b><br>
<br>
2. Tax years. Does it contain the reassessed values for tax year 2026? Can =
it also include the tax year 2025 values (1968 base year), in the same file=
 or as a second file?
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">2 files needed for multiple tax years</spa=
n></b>. <b>
<span style=3D"color:#EE0000">2026 file shows value on day of file run. 202=
5 file would be the final value at EOY. This would be the last value prior =
to the new reassessed values</span></b><br>
<br>
3. Certified versus current values. Are the 2026 values as certified in Nov=
ember 2025 for billing, or as they stand today after appeals? If only curre=
nt values are available, is there a field showing which parcels were change=
d on appeal?
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">Current Value only</span></b><br>
<br>
4. Other fields. Does the extract include: <br>
- parcel ID<br>
- municipality and school district<br>
- property class or land-use code<br>
- exemption status or code, and taxable value<br>
- homestead/farmstead exclusion status<br>
- property address<br>
- owner name and mailing address<br>
- lot size or acreage <br>
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">Yes. Land SqFt and Acreage if available</s=
pan></b><br>
<br>
5. Code tables. Does it come with a data dictionary or code tables for the =
class and exemption codes?
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">Yes</span></b><br>
<br>
6. Format and scope. Is the file CSV or Excel? Is it countywide, or can it =
be limited to the City of Scranton? Either one works for me. A list of the =
column names, or a few sample rows, would answer most of these questions at=
 once.
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">County Wide</span></b><br>
<br>
7. Cost and timing. With email delivery, is $600 the total cost? About how =
long after the check arrives does the file go out?
<b><span style=3D"color:#EE0000">$600 per tax year</span></b>. <b><span sty=
le=3D"color:#EE0000">Within a few days.</span></b><br>
<br>
Thank you for your help.<br>
<br>
Best regards,<br>
