<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-a=
lt:auto">Dear Ms. Harte,<br>
<br>
Under the Pennsylvania Right-to-Know Law, 65 P.S. =A7 67.101 et seq., I req=
uest electronic copies of the records below. A completed Standard Right-to-=
Know Request Form is attached; the numbered list here is the full descripti=
on of records.<br>
<br>
1. An electronic export (CSV, Excel, or whatever electronic format the Asse=
ssment Office's iasWorld system already produces) of the real property asse=
ssment roll for every parcel in the City of Scranton, in these versions:<br=
>
a. the roll certified on or about November 14, 2025 for tax year 2026 (reas=
sessed values), as certified to the City of Scranton for 2026 billing;<br>
b. the roll as it currently stands, if it differs from (a) because of court=
 appeals or other changes after certification;<br>
c. the roll certified for tax year 2025 (1968 base year).<br>
<br>
For each parcel, the following fields, where they are maintained:<br>
- parcel identifier (PIN and map/parcel number);<br>
- municipality and school district;<br>
- property class / land-use code;<br>
- land assessed value, building (improvement) assessed value, and total ass=
essed value;<br>
- exempt value and exemption code (full and partial), and taxable value;<br=
>
- homestead / farmstead exclusion approval status, and the year approved;<b=
r>
- property (situs) address;<br>
- owner name and owner mailing address;<br>
- lot size / acreage;<br>
- whether an informal review, Board of Assessment appeal, or Court of Commo=
n Pleas appeal was filed, its status or decision, its decision date, and th=
e values before and after the appeal.<br>
<br>
2. The certified total of taxable assessed value that the County certified =
to the City of Scranton for tax year 2026, and any revised or supplemental =
certification issued after it.<br>
<br>
3. The code tables or data dictionary needed to read the fields above.<br>
<br>
This is a request for data held in an existing database, not for the creati=
on of a new record. Electronic copies by email or download link are preferr=
ed. If any portion of a record is withheld, please identify the exemption r=
elied on and release the remainder.
 If fees are expected to exceed $50, please contact me before processing.<b=
r>
<br>
Thank you,<br>
<br>
Russell Richie<br>
736 Annin St.<br>
Philadelphia, PA 19147<br>
